  body: "# Referral of a pensions forfeiture question\n\n## Source-backed proposal\n\nThe chapter distinguishes
    the DM deciding whether a forfeiture question arises from referral through Decision Making and Appeals Leeds
    to the Upper Tribunal for determination.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nAn acquittal is not treated by the captured
    guidance as eliminating every referral question. The circumstances, unlawful-killing evidence, potential benefit
    advantage and burden of proof remain separate matters. Do not infer facts from media reports or make an automated
    adverse decision.\n\n## Inspected passages\n\n- [DMG 76013, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a81fada40f0b6230269a321/dmgch76.pdf#page=5).\n\
    - [DMG 76015, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a81fada40f0b6230269a321/dmgch76.pdf#page=5).\n\
    - [DMG 76016, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a81fada40f0b6230269a321/dmgch76.pdf#page=5).\n\
    \n## Provenance and review\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of DWP guidance, not an official DWP document.
    All definitions and relationships are model-assisted and unreviewed. No individual eligibility, award, legal
    conclusion or executable rule is supplied.\n\nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, stated
    legal date and pension event date have separate meanings. PDF page numbers are one-based file positions; extraction
    may damage reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n-
    `dmg-vol12-ch76` — PDF SHA-256 `074f2d3f00d4886954d5cbd6ba2653ec407c1ff9f0160a0ca74d337227f9f542`; page-extraction
    SHA-256 `53eb7c5ec81ced813ac2faf2af9f772c5f3e9662112a7ef678dcb4daef0b73f8`.\n"
