      quote: "76013   In most cases it will be for the DM to decide if a forfeiture rule question arises. If it\n\
        \        does, the DM should refer the case to DMA Leeds who will refer the case to the UT\n        to decide
        the question1 (see DMG 76015).\n                                                                       \
        \      1 TP (UT) Rules, Rule 26(1)"
      locator: DMG 76013
  - target: term/dmg-burden-of-proof
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The referral passage expressly places the onus of proving unlawful killing on the DM.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol12-ch76/0005
      quote: "76015   DMA Leeds will refer cases to the UT. In addition to those cases in DMG 76014, all\n     \
        \   cases should be referred to DMA Leeds to consider reference to the UT where\n\n        1.     a reference
        has been made to the DM to consider the effect of the forfeiture\n               rule and\n\n        2.\
        \     the claimant has been charged with and acquitted of an offence outlined in\n               DMG 76003.\n\
        \n        It is the circumstances of the unlawful killing and not the conviction which gives rise\n    \
        \                   1\n        to a reference . The onus of proving that a killing was unlawful will be
        on the DM.\n                                                                                           \
        \ 1 R(G) 2/90"
      locator: DMG 76015
